    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Severe aplastic anemia: pancytopenia with a low reticulocyte count, confirmed by a hypocellular bone marrow; attributed to cumulative occupational ionizing radiation; linked to the documented 1934 diagnosis: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Occupational exposure to ionizing radiation over decades of radium research and X-ray work: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Chronic radiodermatitis of the fingertips, with thin, scarred skin: active, confirmed [S]</item></list><paragraph>Coordinated follow-up with the primary clinician is appropriate. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Initial anemia workup in primary care: CBC with differential and reticulocyte count, blood film, vitamin B12, folate, ferritin, LDH, bilirubin, and kidney function. Guideline: Guidelines for the diagnosis and management of adult aplastic anaemia: A British Society for Haematology Guideline (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, anemia and cataract monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Supportive care: irradiated, leukocyte-depleted red cells for symptomatic anemia; platelet thresholds set by hematology; same-day assessment for a temperature of 38 °C or higher; avoid aspirin and NSAIDs. Guideline: Guidelines for the diagnosis and management of adult aplastic anaemia: A British Society for Haematology Guideline (2024) [S]</item><item>Record cumulative occupational radiation exposure, stop further exposure while counts recover, and review shielding and dosimetry for laboratory staff with occupational health. Guideline: Guidelines for the diagnosis and management of adult aplastic anaemia: A British Society for Haematology Guideline (2024) [S]</item><item>First-line immunosuppressive therapy given by hematology: horse antithymocyte globulin with cyclosporine and eltrombopag, plus acyclovir prophylaxis; inactivated vaccines only. Guideline: Guidelines for the diagnosis and management of adult aplastic anaemia: A British Society for Haematology Guideline (2024) [S]</item><item>Monitor CBC weekly during the first months of treatment, with kidney function, potassium, and ALT every two weeks on cyclosporine and eltrombopag. Guideline: Guidelines for the diagnosis and management of adult aplastic anaemia: A British Society for Haematology Guideline (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, anemia and cataract monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Comprehensive dilated eye examination with best-corrected acuity, intraocular pressure, slit-lamp examination, and a functional vision assessment; YAG laser capsulotomy when capsule opacification limits daily tasks; eye examinations every one to two years afterward. Guideline: Cataract in the Adult Eye Preferred Practice Pattern (2021); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, anemia and cataract monographs (2026) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
